# The Windows package and the WSL environment share the same working tree, but
# the two gits are configured differently: the Windows one ships with
# core.autocrlf=true from the installer and converts LF->CRLF on checkout, while
# the WSL one does not convert and sees those CRLFs as uncommitted changes. The
# result was 13 "modified" files after every branch switch, differing only in
# line endings, which blocked cherry-picks and merges.
#
# This pins normalisation to LF for all text, whichever git touches the tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# I .bat vivono nel repository, quindi l'eccezione che il commento precedente
# dichiarava non necessaria ora lo e': cmd.exe tollera LF solo in parte -- i
# blocchi multi-riga e i goto no.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.npy binary
